{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 127, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 1->3 is absent, adding the 0->3 skip often restores the only path to the output (exps 19, 20), giving huge gains."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0->3 when edge 1->3 is already none can disconnect the output and collapse accuracy (exps 64, 65)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the 0->3 shortcut, edge 1->3 is a critical path to the output, so removing it hurts much more (exps 32, 33)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 2->3 is absent, node 3 depends heavily on edge 1->3, so deleting it is far more damaging (exps 32, 34)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 1->3 missing, adding a conv on 2->3 can reconnect a dead output and adds the main learnable path (exp 8)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0->2 is none, cutting 0->1 starves nodes 1 and 2 entirely, which hurts much more (exps 92, 93, 99)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where there was no edge adds a path and capacity, whereas replacing an existing conv_3x3 removes capacity (exp 77 vs 73)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an absent 0->1 edge can activate a dead branch, while replacing an existing op only swaps one op for another (exp 30)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "hi